WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.052
Step 1. Open the encounter.

1.2
00:00:02.052 --> 00:00:07.526
You record a procedure in an open encounter of the patient, from the Overview tab.

1.3
00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:12.432
A procedure records something that was done, not done, or stopped.

2.1
00:00:12.432 --> 00:00:17.416
Step 2. Open the Procedure form. Select the Procedures quick action.

2.2
00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:23.348
You can also press C, or select Add Procedure in the Encounter Actions dialog.

3.1
00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:28.693
Step 3. Search for the procedure. Type its name in the Add Procedure search.

3.2
00:00:28.693 --> 00:00:32.649
The search uses the Procedure value set of your deployment,

3.3
00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:35.161
which is SNOMED CT by default.

4.1
00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:39.866
Step 4. Select the procedure. Care adds a new row to the form.

4.2
00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:45.468
The row starts with the status Completed and the outcome Not Specified.

5.1
00:00:45.468 --> 00:00:49.731
Step 5. Set the values of the procedure. Set the outcome.

5.2
00:00:49.731 --> 00:00:52.547
Then open the row menu for more details,

5.3
00:00:52.547 --> 00:01:00.066
such as an approximate date when you do not know the exact day, and a note.

6.1
00:01:00.066 --> 00:01:05.266
Step 6. Add more procedures. Search again to add another procedure.

6.2
00:01:05.266 --> 00:01:09.017
Each procedure gets its own row in the form.

7.1
00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:12.593
Step 7. Save the procedures. Select Save Changes.

7.2
00:01:12.593 --> 00:01:14.969
Care saves the procedures together,

7.3
00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:19.270
and shows them in the Procedures panel of the encounter.
